    "id": "page:index-html:accelerating-enterprise-agentic-ai-adoption",
    "page": "index.html",
    "section": "Accelerating Enterprise Agentic AI Adoption",
    "content": "CyberSec Ops\nMicrosoft Power Platform, PEGA & BPM Platforms\nBusiness Process Intelligence powered by Skan.ai\nEnterprise AI adoption stalls at the gap between platform capability and operational execution. Vikat.AI closes that gap — with consulting depth, embedded IP, and measurable outcomes.\nRSAC 2026 // Agentic Security Brief\nThe Agentic Control Plane is now the defining challenge in enterprise security.\nNo single vendor governs the whole agent chain. Microsoft, Cisco, and Check Point are each building for their own ecosystem — not yours. The control plane has to be engineered for how your enterprise actually operates.\n99.4% AI/SaaS incidents\n79% Zero agent visibility\n22s Attacker handoff\n↓ Download the Whitepaper\nMicrosoft Agent 365 // May 1, 2026\nAgent 365 governs Microsoft agents. But your enterprise doesn't run on Microsoft alone.\nSalesforce agents, AWS automations, custom-built agents, shadow deployments — Agent 365 doesn't see them. The control plane your enterprise needs is a bespoke solution engineered around your entire agent landscape.\n$15 Per user/mo\n1B+ Entra identities\nMay 1 GA date\n↓ Agent 365 Analysis\nCISO Brief // The Accountability Gap\nYour board will ask 5 questions about AI agents this year. Most CISOs can't answer the first one.\nHow many agents are active? Who authorized their access to regulated data? If one goes rogue at 2am, who's accountable? The next AI breach won't end a career because of missing tools — but because of missing answers.\n79% No visibility\n90% Loosened controls\n82→14% Confidence gap\n→ Book CISO Assessment\nPartnership Announcement // 2026\nVikat.AI and Skan.ai partner to bring Agentic Process Intelligence to the enterprise.\nTogether, Vikat.AI consulting depth and Skan.ai's process mining platform deliver end-to-end visibility into how enterprise work actually happens — and the automation roadmap to make it measurably better.\n15–35% Cycle-time reduction\n20–40% Manual effort cut\n90 Day Visibility to value\n→ Explore the Partnership\nWhitepaper // Agent Control Plane\nThe Agent Control Plane: Why every enterprise needs one and how to build it.\nAI agents are multiplying across your enterprise stack. Without a unified control plane — governing identity, access, execution, and accountability — each agent is an ungoverned risk. This whitepaper maps the architecture every CISO needs in 2026.\n40% Apps with agents by 2026\n6% Have AI security strategy\n2026 Board liability year\n↓ Download the Whitepaper\n‹\n›\nSchedule a Briefing →\nExplore What We Do\nPartnerships & Enterprise Security Platforms We Work With\n01 — Security for the Agentic Enterprise"
